Summary: List of intrinsics obtained by eating.
Keywords: Eating = Intrinsics list

Hello, all.
There have been several posts recently asking for a list of what corpses
provide which intrinsics.  Since no one else has posted such a list, I have
decided to do so.  Here it is:

There is a menu here.  Read it (ynq)?

DISCLAIMER:  I am not a member of the dev team, nor have I looked at the 
source code.  I am merely an experienced player working from memory.  So,
this list may not be entirely complete or totally accurate...

Note that most monster species do not automatically give you intrinsics.
There is a _chance_ to gain intrinsics by eating corpses, but it is not 
certain for most types.  However, if intrinsic gain _is_ certain for eating
a monster type, then that is indicated by (always) after the monster name.

"You feel healthy." - poison resistance.
Any poisonous insect or snake, cave spiders, brown or black puddings, gray
oozes, shriekers, green dragons (always), unicorns.  Warning:  poisonous
monsters leave poisonous corpses!

"You feel wide awake." - sleep resistance.
Elves (any type), orange dragons (always), homunculi, possibly acid blobs?
(acid blobs are an unverified rumor...)

"You feel full of hot air." - cold resistance.
Blue jellies, winter wolves, yetis, white dragons (always), possibly anything
else with a cold-based attack, brown or black puddings.

"You feel a momentary chill." - fire resistance.
Red molds, red dragons (always), brown or black puddings, possibly anything
else with a fiery attack (like hell hounds).

"Your health currently feels amplified." - shock resistance.
Brown or black puddings, blue dragons (always).

"You feel very firm." - disintegration resistance.
Black dragons (always)

"You feel a strange mental acuity." - telepathy.
Floating eye (always), or mind flayer (see below).

"Yum.  That was real brain food!  You feel smart!" - +1 INT.
Mind flayer.  These always give you something:  intrinsic telepathy if you
don't already have it, extra INT if you do!

"You feel a change coming over you." - polymorph.
Chameleon (always).  Intrinsic random polymorph... ugh!  Goes away after a
while, though.

"You feel hidden." - intrinsic see invisible AND intrinsic invisibility.
Invisible stalker.  These will always give you something.  If you are not
invisible, you will temporarily become so.  If you are invisible, by any 
means, you will get BOTH listed intrinsics, permanently!  Warning:  will
stun you.

"You feel more experienced." - +1 level.
Wraiths (always)!  :-)

"You feel very jumpy." - teleport.
Nymphs (any type), leprechauns, or tengus.

"You feel in control of yourself." - teleport control.
Tengus.

(no message) - aggravate monster.
kitten/housecat/large cat or little dog/dog/large dog.

(no message) - loss of intrinsics!
gremlins?  (unconfirmed)

"Your velocity seems very uncertain." - change in speed.
Quantum mechanic (always).  Speeds you if you are slow, but slows you if you
are fast!  Warning:  poisonous (in NH 3.0), possibly not in 3.1

"You will be punished for this act of cannibalism!" (or something similar...)
This is a BIG mistake.  Your luck will drop through the floor, and your god
will *not* be amused.  Any @ except elves (unless you're an elf).  Also,
Keystone Kops may count as people. (unconfirmed)

"This makes you feel like Popeye!" or (no message) - gain strength.
Tin of spinach (gives you the message), royal jelly (from beehive), or
giant corpses.  Giants give you multiple points!  (Stone giants yield the 
most...usually 10+ points.)

Whew!  I think that's all of them...
